46(00)90033-8</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Soslowsky LJ, Thomopoulos S, Tun S, Flanagan CL, Keefer CC, Mastaw J, Carpenter JE. Neer Award 1999. Overuse activity injures the supraspinatus tendon in an animal model: a histologic and biomechanical study. J Shoulder Elbow Surg. 2000;9:79&#x02013;84. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10810684</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wall</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Banes</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Early responses to mechanical load in tendon: role for calcium signaling, gap junctions and intercellular communication</article-title><source>J Musculoskelet Neuronal Interact</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>70</fpage><lpage>84</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Wall ME, Banes AJ. Early responses to mechanical load in tendon: role for calcium signaling, gap junctions and intercellular communication. J Musculoskelet Neuronal Interact. 2005;5:70&#x02013;84. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15788873</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanobiology of tendon</article-title><source>J Biomech</source><year>2006</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>1563</fpage><lpage>1582</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jbiomech.2005.05.011</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Wang JH. Mechanobiology of tendon. J Biomech. 2006;39:1563&#x02013;1582. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16000201</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn><p>One or more of the authors (SPL, LJS) have received funding from the National Institutes of Health, Wyeth Research, and the National Scien